@title Checkout Payment Flow v2
@subtitle In-app checkout design, Tidewater Grocers
@author Payments Engineering
@date 2026-09-22

## Payment sequence

diagram pay sequence title="Checkout payment sequence"
pay: app "Mobile App" user
pay: checkout "Checkout API" svc
pay: fraud "Fraud Service" svc
pay: gateway "Payment Gateway" ext
pay: ledger "Ledger" db
pay: app -> checkout : POST /checkout with cart and card token
pay: checkout -> fraud : score order
pay: fraud --> checkout : risk score
pay: note checkout : alt: risk score above 80
pay: checkout --> app : step-up verification required
pay: note checkout : stop here, Payment Gateway is not called
pay: note checkout : else: risk score 80 or below
pay: checkout -> gateway : authorize amount
pay: gateway --> checkout : auth code
pay: checkout -> ledger : record pending charge
pay: ledger --> checkout : entry id
pay: checkout --> app : order confirmed

If the fraud risk score is above 80, Checkout API answers the Mobile App with **step-up verification required** and never calls the Payment Gateway. Otherwise the flow continues to authorization and the ledger write.

## Latency budget

data latency = Step,p95 budget (ms),Measured p95 (ms); Fraud scoring,120,96; Authorization,450,512; Ledger write,40,31; Total checkout,800,811
table latency
chart bar latency x=Step y=p95 budget (ms),Measured p95 (ms) unit=ms title="p95 budget vs measured"

## Open issues

!! **Authorization is 62 ms over budget** (512 ms measured vs 450 ms budget) because the gateway's us-east endpoint is called from us-west-2. Total checkout p95 is 811 ms against an 800 ms budget.

Next steps:

- Move to the gateway's regional endpoint.
- Add a 2 second timeout with one retry.
- Alert when total checkout p95 exceeds 800 ms.
